  "behaviours": {
    "async_jobs": "pyvo (`AsyncTAPJob`) and astroquery (`TapPlus`) each submit an async TAP query to CADC, IRSA, ARI and MAST, wait for the job to end and fetch its result.",
    "datalink_cutout": "a cutout gets the pixels around a target without downloading the whole image. pyvo (`DatalinkRecord.processed`) and astroquery (`Cadc.get_image_list`) each take one CADC image from its ObsCore table, follow the image's DataLink to its `#cutout` SODA service and ask for a circle of radius 0.1° around the image centre.",
    "error_documents": "a failed query is the most common thing users hit, and the service's own error message is what tells them why. pyvo (`TAPService.run_sync`) and astroquery (`TapPlus.launch_job`) each send CADC, IRSA, ARI and MAST a sync TAP query on a table that does not exist. The check first fetches the service's raw error response and takes its message: the text of the `QUERY_STATUS` `ERROR` INFO when the response is a VOTable, or the whole body otherwise."
  },
  "run_at": "2026-10-25T14:47:42Z",
  "source": "https://github.com/caliperforge/vo-conformance/tree/main/results",
  "definition": "Every row of caliperforge/vo-conformance results/<day>.jsonl for the 30 UTC days to today, in file order: the day, the client, the service, the behaviour, its outcome (pass, fail or not supported) and its note. behaviours holds the README description of each behaviour in the rows, and run_at the commit time of the newest results file.",
  "caveat": "A day the daily run committed no results file has no rows. Notes are as the runner wrote them, and null where it wrote none."
}